<title>LITHUANIA: SOCGEN SAYS CONSIDERING BRANCH.</title>
<headline>SOCGEN SAYS CONSIDERING BRANCH.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>French banking giant Societe Generale said on Thursday that it was looking to see whether it would open a branch office in Lithuania.</p>
<p>&quot;We confirm we study the possibility to open a branch office in Lithuania,&quot; Denis Davidoff, area manager CIS and Baltic countries, told Reuters.  </p>
<p>He confirmed that he earlier met the Bank of Lithuania and that this was the beginning of its investigations of the market.</p>
<p>Societe Generale already has an office in Latvian capital, Riga.</p>
<p>The only other foreign bank with an office in Lithuania is Poland's Kredyt Bank.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 223 517</p>
